Sequence feature extraction is the foundation of most machine learning methods, including multi-label learning. From some literature4 we know that the amino acid composition (AAC) is the most important factor for peptide classification and design, so it may be a good choice. AAC is defined as the 20-dimensional feature vector consists of the frequencies of different amino acids, and it has been successfully used for many protein classification problems25–27. Concretely, given an amino acid sequence P with L in length,1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\bf{P}}={{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{1}}}{{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{2}}}{{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{3}}}{{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{4}}}{{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{5}}}{{\rm{A}}}_{{\rm{6}}}{{\rm{\ldots }}A}_{L}$$\end{document}P=A1A2A3A4A5A6…ALwhere A1 is the first amino acid residue in sequence, A2 is the second one, and so forth. This sequence can be represented as the AAC vector as [a1, a2, …, a20]T, in which ai (i = 1, 2, …, 20) are the occurrence frequencies of the 20 native amino acids, and T is the transpose operator.

There is a material weakness for representing AMPs as AAC only because no sequence order information is considered. So the dipeptide composition (DC)28,29, the frequencies of different dipeptides (combinations of two adjacent amino acids), is also used to represent AMP sequence. The DC is a 400-dimensional vector as [d1, d2, …, d400]T, in which di (i = 1, 2, …, 400) is the occurrence frequency of the ith dipeptide. Now any AMP sequence can be converted to a 420-dimensional feature vector as below,2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\boldsymbol{x}}={[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},\ldots ,{x}_{20},{x}_{21},{x}_{22},\ldots ,{x}_{420}]}^{{\rm{T}}}$$\end{document}x=[x1,x2,…,x20,x21,x22,…,x420]Tin which the first twenty features are AAC and the other ones are DC.

